  "description": "An EMPTY result. TRANSACT exists at its declared 350-byte width and holds no row, which is a different assertion from a case that never mentions the dataset - only this one reaches the first-read end-of-data branch. STARTBR positions at LOW-VALUES and its probe read finds nothing, so STARTBR-TRANSACT-FILE takes its end-of-data arm at :605-611: SET TRANSACT-EOF, 'You are at the top of the page...', MOVE -1 TO TRNIDINL, SEND. Note what that arm does NOT do - it never sets WS-ERR-FLG - which is why :283 still lets execution continue. The blanking loop at :289 is skipped because TRANSACT-EOF is already true, the paging loop makes no iteration, and at :316 WS-IDX is still 1 so 'IF WS-IDX > 1' is FALSE and the page number stays ZERO. An implementation that bumped it unconditionally would show page one over an empty list. MAIN-PARA's first-entry branch performs BOTH PROCESS-ENTER-KEY at :115 AND SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN at :116, so this path sends one more time than PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD does on its own - the last send is :116's and it re-paints the same screen with WS-MESSAGE unchanged.",
